{
  "_doc": [
    "The Gradient slider's law (transcripts/GRADIENT.md, The slider law (precisely)).",
    "Each vector names an op: add_stop(stops, location) and delete_stop(stops, index) and drag_stop(stops, index, location, dy) return {stops, index} (the selected stop afterwards); set_midpoint(stops, pair, value) and drag_midpoint(stops, pair, location) return {stops}. expected: null means refused, nothing written.",
    "Every expected value was computed by hand from the spec text before the reference law existed; each _comment shows the arithmetic.",
    "Stops use the YAML shape {color, opacity, location, midpoint_to_next}. Input stops mostly carry midpoint_to_next 40 so a reset to 50 is visible.",
    "Read by workspace_interpreter/tests/test_gradient_slider.py (reference), jas_dioxus/src/cross_language_test.rs and JasSwift/Tests/Panels/GradientStopCorpusTests.swift."
  ],
  "vectors": [
    {
      "name": "add_between_at_half_midpoint",
      "op": "add_stop",
      "_comment": "t = 0.25, m = 0.5, so u = 0.25: red 255 -> 191.25 -> 191 (bf), blue 63.75 -> 64 (40), opacity 100 -> 0 at u 0.25 is 75. The left stop's next changed, so its midpoint resets (it was already 50).",
      "stops": [
        {
          "color": "#ff0000",
          "opacity": 100,
          "location": 0,
          "midpoint_to_next": 50
        },
        {
          "color": "#0000ff",
          "opacity": 0,
          "location": 100,
          "midpoint_to_next": 50
        }
      ],
      "location": 25,
      "expected": {
        "stops": [
          {
            "color": "#ff0000",
            "opacity": 100,
            "location": 0,
            "midpoint_to_next": 50
          },
          {
            "color": "#bf0040",
            "opacity": 75,
            "location": 25,
            "midpoint_to_next": 50
          },
          {
            "color": "#0000ff",
            "opacity": 0,
            "location": 100,
            "midpoint_to_next": 50
          }
        ],
        "index": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "add_honours_the_midpoint_below_it",
      "op": "add_stop",
      "_comment": "m = 0.25 and t = 0.1 < m, so u = 0.5 * 0.4 = 0.2: red 255 - 51 = 204 (cc), blue 51 (33). A law that ignores the midpoint gives u = 0.1 (#e6001a).",
      "stops": [
        {
          "color": "#ff0000",
          "opacity": 100,
          "location": 0,
          "midpoint_to_next": 25
        },
        {
          "color": "#0000ff",
          "opacity": 100,
          "location": 100,
          "midpoint_to_next": 40
        }
      ],
      "location": 10,
